Is there another form of switch?

Yes — switch expressions (arrow syntax, ->, with yield), introduced in Java 14. Example:

```java
int result = switch (day) {
    case 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 -> "Weekday";
    case 6, 7 -> "Weekend";
    default -> "Invalid";
};
```

I called the one we covered "classic switch" deliberately — because this arrow-based version is a Java 8+ feature (technically Java 12–14), and you asked to keep modern Java features out of this syllabus. So it's intentionally excluded here, not forgotten. If you want, we can note it exists for now and cover it properly later when you decide to do the modern-Java module.


